WEBVTT

NOTE
This audio description covers Squall separated in Time Compression.
Duration: approximately 15 seconds
Scene: Squall wanders alone through a shifting void of compressed time.
For blind players: Descriptions focus on disorientation, memory flashes, and environmental instability.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Squall is alone. The young SeeD commander floats in a void that is neither fully solid nor fully empty. Around him, the compressed timeline manifests as a landscape that cannot decide what it is. One moment he stands in a vast desert, sand dunes stretching to a horizon that is too close. The next moment, the desert dissolves into ocean — he sees water beneath him, around him, above him, all at once. He looks down and sees waves. He looks up and sees more waves.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Flashes of memory erupt through the chaos. He sees Rinoa's face, clear and real for just an instant — her smile, her eyes, her hand reaching toward him. The vision dissipates like smoke. A field of white flowers fills his vision, the same field where they first danced together at the Ball. But it too fades, replaced by the endless ocean. The memories are his anchor, his tether to his own timeline, but they slip through his fingers.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Squall staggers through environments that shift without warning. Grass beneath his feet becomes cold stone becomes sand becomes water becomes nothing. The landscape cycles faster and faster — forests blur into cities blur into mountains blur into the starfield itself. He is disoriented, struggling to find solid ground, to find reality, to find his way back to his friends. His hand reaches out, grasping at the shifting air. His voice calls out, but the sound is swallowed by the void. He is fighting not just against an external enemy, but against the fundamental dissolution of his own existence.
